/* Built by tools/build_pages.py: the help centre's search index, read in the browser by help.js. */
window.HELP_INDEX = [{"u":"owners.html","t":"Getting started as an owner","s":"Create your workspace, add clients and people, and get the first tasks moving in about ten minutes.","c":"Getting started","k":"owner new workspace setup first steps trial invite onboarding checklist","b":"Open the app and choose Create an account . Confirm your email from the message Handlark sends. Name your workspace (usually your business), answer What kind of team are you? and choose your time zone for deadlines. See Your kind of team . Your free trial starts at once: 14 days, or 44 days if a customer invited you, with up to 15 people and no card. The workspace starts with sample clients and templates so the screens are not empty. Rename them or delete them when you are ready. Go to Settings, Clients and choose New client . A client has a type: Client for outside customers (time is billable by default) or Internal for your own work (not billable by default). Open a client to set its hourly rate, currency, client email and client page link. Go to Settings, People and choose New person . Type their name and email and save. If email is set up they get an invitation; either way you can copy their invite link and send it yourself, for example on WhatsApp. Invite links work for 14 days. Give each person a role: Member , Team lead or Manager . See Roles and teams . Use the plus button ( New task ) and choose who it is for, the client, a due date and the priority. The person sees it on their Home straight away. Tick Needs my sign off if you want to check the work before it counts as done. Phone alerts for yourself: Settings, Alerts, calendar and sign in , then Turn on for this device . Daily summary email : Settings, Emails and deadlines . Two step sign in , and require it for everyone under Settings, Security . Get paid online with your own Paystack account, so clients pay invoices by card, transfer or USSD. Accept the data processing agreement under Settings, Data processing agreement if your clients or your own policy need one."},{"u":"managers.html","t":"Getting started as a manager","s":"What a manager can do, which people you look after, and the three extra rights an owner can grant.","c":"Getting started","k":"manager role grants rates billing settings approve","b":"Add people (as members) and change the people you look after, including their hours, weekly hour limit, country for public holidays and leave allowance. Approve timesheets, leave, expense claims, time claims and shift swaps for the people you look after. Plan shifts, see attendance, time, review flags and the Insights for your people. Edit or remove someone's time and clock records. Under Settings, People , the owner can tick three switches for you, each on its own: Rates and pay (pay and bill rates, payroll, payouts), Invoices and client billing (invoices, client pages, client emails and rates) and Workspace settings (work sites, holidays, leave types, attendance, hour limits, webhooks and chat alerts). The plan and its payments, the history of changes, export everything, two step sign in for everyone, the Paystack key and Proof mode. Your own requests go to the owner, never to yourself."},{"u":"team_leads.html","t":"Getting started as a team lead","s":"Approve your team's time and leave, plan their shifts and keep an eye on attendance, without any money settings.","c":"Getting started","k":"team lead approve timesheets leave swaps","b":"Timesheets, leave, expense claims, time claims and shift swaps from your team come to you first. Find them under Insights (Time, Expenses, Schedule, Leave and holidays) and on the line at the top of Home when something waits. Plan shifts for your team under Insights, Schedule, Plan shifts . If a shift starts without a clock in, the person is told first and can give a reason; you hear only if nothing is explained in time. You see hours, billable hours, utilization, capacity and the unusual time report for your team. Focus and meeting time show only as one total for everyone you look after, when that is three or more people, and wellbeing only as counts. See Kind insights ."},{"u":"members.html","t":"Getting started as a member","s":"Your Home, your tasks, the timer and the time clock: everything you need on your first day.","c":"Getting started","k":"member assistant first day home tasks timer clock","b":"Open the invite link your owner sent, create an account with any email and a password, and you land in the workspace. If you already have an account, sign in and the workspace appears. Home greets you, shows a line about your own day (a meeting soon, something waiting for you, or a short tip), the time clock, today's schedule and your clients. See Home and team time . Open a task to read it, tick its steps, post a progress update or ask a question. Start the timer on the task while you work, or start a focus session. When you finish, choose Mark done and add one line on what you did, a link or a file. Use Clock in on Home when your working day starts, Take a break for breaks, and Clock out with a short handoff note. See The time clock . Tap your initials (on a computer, Settings) for your account: phone alerts, your language, your calendar link, two step sign in, leave, payout details, API tokens, the browser extension and export."},{"u":"team_type.html","t":"Your kind of team","s":"Service firm, company, remote team or NGO: what the choice changes, the words for a client, and turning billing on or off.","c":"Getting started","k":"kind of team type company department ngo project field service firm agency remote outsourcing we bill clients billing hidden","b":"Service firm or agency : you serve clients, such as accounting, law, consulting or a creative agency. Work is grouped by client, with client pages, rates and invoices. Remote or outsourcing team : you serve clients from elsewhere, such as a virtual assistant agency. The same as a service firm. Company or growing team : your own work. A client is called a Department , and the sample work starts with Operations, Sales and Admin. NGO or field team : projects across locations. A client is called a Project , and work sites and attendance come first in Settings and Insights. Workspaces made before version 1.16.0 are service firms, so nothing changed for them. For a company or an NGO, Bill hours , invoices, rates, retainers and the billing parts of the client page stay out of the menus. If you do bill someone, turn on We bill clients under Settings, Workspace, Kind of team . Nothing is deleted or switched off either way: an invoice made earlier is still there. The owner, or a manager allowed workspace settings, changes the kind of team under Settings, Workspace, Kind of team and chooses Save kind of team . The words change at once for everyone, in English and French. Names you typed, such as a department called Client Services, never change. The history of changes records who changed it."},{"u":"clients.html","t":"For clients: your client page","s":"Follow progress, comment, approve finished work and hours, pay invoices and ask for work or meetings, with no account.","c":"Getting started","k":"client page portal approve hours pay invoice request meeting no login","b":"Work in progress and finished work for you, comments, meetings you are invited to, invoices and, if the team chose, your hours this month and in all, a monthly retainer and a detailed timesheet. You never see private notes kept inside the team. The page shows in your browser's language: English or French. Type your name at the top of the page so the team knows who commented or approved. It is kept on your device for next time. For finished work, choose Approve , or comment if something needs changing. If the team asks you to approve hours, each line shows the date, first name, task and hours: choose Approve , or Query and say what looks wrong. The team replies on the page. Only approved hours are billed. Open the invoice and choose Pay now to pay by card, bank transfer or USSD through Paystack, in naira, cedis, rand, Kenyan shillings or US dollars. You can pay part of it. The invoice updates straight away. If you paid another way, choose I have paid by transfer . Request something puts new work straight onto the team's list. Ask for a meeting lets you suggest up to three times; the team picks one and you get the link. For meetings you are invited to, say whether you can make it and join from the page."},{"u":"roles.html","t":"Roles and teams","s":"Owner, Manager, Team lead and Member: who sees and does what, and how teams send requests to the right person.","c":"Getting started","k":"role permission matrix team lead manager member owner looks after hidden","b":"Role Does Owner Everything, including the plan, the history, export everything, two step sign in for everyone, the Paystack key and Proof mode Manager People, tasks, approvals, shifts and reports for everyone or chosen teams; rates, billing and settings only when granted Team lead Approvals, shifts, time and attendance for their team's members; no money and no people settings Member Their own work Clients are never users: they keep their private client page link. Under Settings, Teams , choose New team , give it a name, one or more team leads and the members. A person can be in several teams. Requests go to the person's team leads first, then a manager who looks after them, then the owner. The owner can hide a person from everyone else. Their work never reaches members, the client page shows them as Team member , and only the owner looks after them."},{"u":"tasks.html","t":"Tasks","s":"New tasks, steps, sign off, repeating work, templates, private tasks, importing from Excel, CSV or Trello, and the bin.","c":"Tasks, time and the clock","k":"task new task steps checklist sign off repeat template import excel csv trello private bin archive priority due","b":"The plus button opens New task . Choose One task , Several (one per line, pasted straight from a message), a Template or From text (AI turns a message or a voice note into tasks, when it is switched on). Give it a client, who it is assigned to, a due date and time, a priority, steps and details. Tasks move through New , In progress , Waiting and Done . With Needs my sign off ticked, finished work goes back to the person who asked for it, who signs it off or sends it back with a note. Marking work done asks for one line on what you did, a link or a file. A task can repeat every day, every weekday, every week or every month; when it is done the next one is made. Templates (owners, under Settings, Templates ) hold a list of steps; a step written as Reconcile bank accounts +2 [2h] falls two days after the start date with a time budget of two hours. If the owner allows it ( Can keep private lists under People), you can keep private tasks and private lists that only you see. They never reach the owner, clients, exports of others, the AI or the API, and their time is never billed. Tasks, Import takes an Excel workbook, a CSV file, cells pasted from a spreadsheet, or a Trello board export. Trello lists are matched to statuses, and checklists become steps. Deleted tasks wait in Tasks, Bin for 30 days and can be restored by the person who made them or the owner. Finished tasks move to Tasks, Archive after 90 days; search and reopen them there."},{"u":"home.html","t":"Home and team time","s":"The line at the top of Home, tips, the team pill, team time, best overlap and quiet hours.","c":"Tasks, time and the clock","k":"home spotlight line tips team pill team time overlap quiet hours time zones greeting","b":"It rotates every 12 seconds: lines about your own day first (a meeting soon, approvals waiting, a question for you, overdue work), with short tips between them. Tap a line to go there. Pause stops it; with reduced motion on in your device it changes only now and then. Switch tips off in your account ( Rotating tips on Home ). The Team pill shows how many people are working now. Tap it for everyone's local time, where their day is and their working hours in your time. Best overlap is the stretch today when most people are working; Set up a meeting in this window books it. Nobody's location is shown, only times. With Respect quiet hours on (the default), phone and WhatsApp alerts to someone outside their working hours wait until their day starts. Urgent alerts never wait: a meeting about to start, the still working check, payments and codes."},{"u":"time_clock.html","t":"The time clock","s":"Clock in and out, breaks, clocking in for a client, switching clients, handoff notes, work sites and location.","c":"Tasks, time and the clock","k":"clock in clock out break shift handoff switch client location work site payroll hours","b":"On Home, Clock in starts your working day; Take a break and End break pause it; Clock out ends it with an optional handoff note that goes into the daily summary. A shift left open for 16 hours closes by itself and is flagged for a check. For a client clocks you in for a client and, if you like, a task. Your hours count for that client until you switch or clock out. Switch client moves the clock without clocking out. Breaks are never billed. Tap a shift under Insights, Time clock to correct its times. A shift with time a client approved needs a reason, and the client is asked again. If the owner left it on, your phone may ask for your location when you clock in or out. Say no and you still clock in. Work sites (owners, Settings, Work sites ) mark a shift Away from site when it is outside the site's radius. Nothing is ever blocked, and members never see anyone else's location."},{"u":"timers.html","t":"Timers, focus sessions and timesheets","s":"Time a task, add time by hand, send your week for approval, and how time budgets and notes work.","c":"Tasks, time and the clock","k":"timer start stop add time manual timesheet week approve budget estimate focus session note","b":"Open a task and choose Start timer . One timer runs at a time: starting another stops the first. If you are clocked in for a client, the clock moves to the task, so nothing counts twice. A timer that runs past 10 hours, or 2 hours past the end of your working day, stops by itself and is flagged. You can also time from the browser extension . Time longer than 30 minutes asks for a line on what you did when it stops. A task can have a time budget set by whoever made it; at 80% you get a gentle nudge, and past 100% adding time asks for a short reason. Your own estimate stays private and is never used to judge you. A focus session is a timed stretch on one task (5 to 50 minutes) with a calm screen and a place to park stray thoughts, which become tasks when it ends. Under Insights, Time, My week , choose Send for approval . Your team lead, a manager or the owner approves it or sends it back with a note. Approved time can be billed."},{"u":"still_working.html","t":"The still working check and the idle check","s":"Why Handlark sometimes asks \"Still working?\", how to answer, and what happens to time when nobody answers.","c":"Tasks, time and the clock","k":"still working check idle paused unconfirmed claim time stopped at","b":"While a timer or the clock runs and nothing has happened in Handlark for a while (45 minutes by default), you get a phone alert or a banner: Still working on ...? Answer Yes, keep going , Pause , or I stopped at a time. After 10 more minutes the time stops at your last activity plus 10 minutes. The gap is kept as unconfirmed time that you can claim with a note; the owner approves it. Time is never silently thrown away, and it is only paused when the question really reached you. If the owner turns it on, the Handlark tab notes only the moment of your last key, click, tap or scroll in that tab, and asks sooner when the tab has been quiet. Choose I often work in other apps and a quiet tab never counts against you. The browser extension offers an idle hint too, only if you switch it on."},{"u":"proof_mode.html","t":"Proof mode","s":"Optional screenshots for one client, only with each person's consent, seen by the person first and deletable.","c":"Tasks, time and the clock","k":"proof mode screenshots consent blurred share screen tray withdraw","b":"Some clients ask for proof of hours. Proof mode is off unless the owner turns it on for that client. It takes 1 to 3 screenshots in each 10 minutes, blurred by default, only in your own browser while you share your screen and time runs for that client. The first time you add time for that client you see exactly what is captured, how often, who sees it and for how long, and you tick I have read this and I agree . The owner can never agree for you. Withdraw in your account stops it: nothing more is captured, and your screenshots for that client are deleted, except ones on time already approved or invoiced, which stay as the evidence for that time until they are deleted as usual. Every screenshot waits in your Proof tray for 10 minutes, where you can delete it. A deleted one leaves only a marker. Pause proof for 10 minutes is there for private moments. Phones cannot share a screen, and the browser extension never captures one, so time for a Proof client starts in the web app on a computer."},{"u":"shifts.html","t":"Planned shifts, attendance and hour limits","s":"Plan shifts once or every week, swap or drop them, see who was on time, and set weekly hour limits and overtime.","c":"People, shifts and leave","k":"shift schedule plan swap drop late missed left early attendance report grace overtime limit","b":"Insights, Schedule, Plan shifts : a person, One day , Every week or Every other week , the days, start and end in that person's own time zone, and optionally a client and a work site. End this plan stops it from today. Swap or drop gives one shift to a teammate or drops it, with a reason. Your lead, a manager or the owner approves it, and both people are told. After a grace period (10 minutes by default), a shift with no clock in is told to you first, with Add reason . Only if nothing is explained within 15 minutes does your team lead hear. Leave and public holidays never count as missed. Under Settings, Attendance and hours , a weekly hour limit gives you a note at 90% and tells your lead past 100%. Overtime rules pay hours past a daily and weekly limit at a multiplier in payroll."},{"u":"leave.html","t":"Leave and public holidays","s":"Ask for leave, see your balances, set leave types and allowances, and holidays for 12 countries.","c":"People, shifts and leave","k":"leave annual sick holiday balance accrual carry over half day public holidays country","b":"In your account choose Ask for leave (or Insights, Leave and holidays ). Pick the type, the dates and, for one day, a half day. The request sheet shows what is left. Your lead, a manager or the owner approves it, and it comes off your balance. Owners set types under Settings, Leave types : days a year, Earned each month or All at the start of the year , a carry over cap, paid or unpaid, and whether it Can go below zero . Balances count working days only. Holidays for Nigeria, Ghana, Kenya, South Africa, Egypt, the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Philippines, India, Pakistan and Bangladesh are worked out for any year, by each person's country. Islamic holidays are marked as possibly moving. Add your own days under Settings ."},{"u":"client_billing.html","t":"Clients, rates and client approval of hours","s":"Client settings, rates and rounding, retainers, client page links and asking clients to approve hours before billing.","c":"Clients, invoices and pay","k":"client rate rounding retainer client link portal approve hours query billable language","b":"Open a client under Settings, Clients : hourly rate and currency, a rate per person, rounding (none, 6, 15 or 30 minutes), billable by default, a monthly retainer in hours or money with alerts at 80% and 100%, the client email and the language of this client's emails (English or French). Create client link makes the private page; send it to the client. Turn off link stops it at once. Choose what it shows: a detailed timesheet, time budgets, a daily summary email and a weekly report on Fridays. Switch on Client approves hours before billing . The client approves or queries each line on their page; you reply under Insights, Time , adjusting minutes if needed. Bill hours then takes only approved lines."},{"u":"invoices.html","t":"Invoices and getting paid","s":"Bill tracked hours, send invoices, take payment online, recurring invoices, reminders, part payments and credit notes.","c":"Clients, invoices and pay","k":"invoice bill hours paystack pay online recurring reminder late fee credit note ageing receivables part payment","b":"Bill hours (Insights, Invoices, a client, or the Time view) makes a draft invoice from approved, unbilled time and locks those entries so they are never billed twice. Delete or void the invoice to free the time again. Connect your own Paystack under Settings, Get paid online and paste the webhook address it shows into Paystack. Clients then pay from their page, and the invoice marks itself paid. The money goes to you, never through Handlark. A payment page works for 24 hours. If the client pays more than is still due (say a credit note lowered the invoice after they opened the page), or pays from a page that has expired, the money is never lost: what is due is applied, the rest is kept as a credit on the client, and you get an email. Find it under Insights, Invoices , Payments to sort out : refund it in Paystack and mark it refunded, or apply it to one of their open invoices, which records it there as a payment. While such a payment waits, that client gets no reminders and no late fees. An invoice is paid when its recorded payments and credits cover it, so removing a payment opens it again, and removing a credit you applied puts that amount back in the client's credit. Recurring makes invoices weekly or monthly from approved hours or a retainer. Under Settings, Reminders, late fees and currencies , turn on friendly reminders on the days you choose and an optional late fee, off by default. Record payment takes part payments; Credit note lowers what is owed. Ageing and Receivables show what clients owe and how late, per currency."},{"u":"payroll.html","t":"Payroll, payouts and payslips","s":"Monthly payroll with overtime and leave, payout files for Wise, PayPal, Payoneer, Deel and Gusto, and paying staff through your own Paystack.","c":"Clients, invoices and pay","k":"payroll pay rate overtime payout wise paypal payoneer deel gusto paystack transfers payslip amounts owed","b":"Insights, Payroll shows monthly hours, overtime, late starts, leave, public holidays and gross pay before tax, with an export. Pay rates are set under Settings, People by the owner or a manager with Rates and pay . Each person adds how they are paid in their account under Payout details . Account numbers are stored encrypted and only the last 4 digits ever show. You get an email whenever your details change. Approve the month with Approve payroll , then make Payout files for Wise, PayPal, Payoneer, Deel or Gusto, or choose Pay people to send pay from your own Paystack balance with a fresh code from your authenticator app. Each person gets a payslip by email once paid. The server works out every amount from the time clock, leave, holidays, rates and approved expenses; if what the page showed differs, approving is refused and you reload. A manager with Rates and pay approves and pays only the people they look after, never themselves: the owner approves and pays a manager. Approving again changes only the lines of the people you look after, so lines the owner approved stay. Payout details someone other than the person changes wait for that person, or the owner, to confirm them (the person gets an email and a note in their account, Payout details); until then nobody is paid to them and they stay out of payout files. A manager never pays, or puts in a file, details they changed themselves. A manager's changes to pay are sent to the owner, and a rise of more than 25% over what the owner last set, a new pay type, a new currency or overtime rules that pay more (a higher multiplier, or overtime starting sooner) wait for the owner to approve them under People. Cuts apply at once. A manager can reopen only the lines of the people they look after whose pay has not gone out; the owner reopens the whole month. Payout details someone other than the person changed in the last 7 days, you included, need a tick that you checked them with the person on a call. Send again repeats a transfer to the same account it was made for; if the details changed since, choose Check status , and when Paystack has no such transfer it is cancelled so you can pay the new account in a new payment."},{"u":"expenses.html","t":"Expenses","s":"Claim expenses with receipts, approve them, repay them in payroll and bill them to clients.","c":"Clients, invoices and pay","k":"expense receipt claim reimburse bill to client","b":"Under Insights, Expenses , choose Add expense , with the amount, client and a photo or PDF of the receipt (up to 10 MB). Your lead, a manager or the owner approves it. Approved expenses are repaid in payroll, and billable ones can go on the client's invoice."},{"u":"insights.html","t":"Kind insights","s":"Overview, focus and meeting time, utilization, capacity, wellbeing signals and unusual time, without watching anyone.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"insights overview focus meetings utilization capacity wellbeing unusual time my patterns export","b":"Owners, managers and team leads see hours, billable hours, utilization, on time against planned shifts, focus and meetings, unusual time and free hours ahead, with Export CSV and Print . Everyone sees their own focus and meeting time, utilization, capacity, unusual time and wellbeing signals first, privately, with a kind suggestion. No app or website tracking, no keyboard or mouse scores and no ranking: people are always listed by name. Leads see focus and meetings only as one total for everyone they look after, when that is three or more people, rounded to the hour, and never for a single team they pick: two teams side by side could give away one person's time. Each person counts only for the time they were in that lead's teams, so moving someone in or out never reveals their earlier time. Wellbeing shows the same way, only as counts, unless a person chooses to share."},{"u":"meetings.html","t":"Meetings","s":"Meetings with free video rooms, agendas, notes that become tasks, reminders, and meetings with clients.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"meeting video jitsi zoom google meet teams agenda notes actions invite calendar","b":"Calendar, Meetings, New meeting : title, time, people, an agenda and the video room. Each meeting gets a free room on meet.jit.si, or paste your own Zoom, Google Meet or Teams link. Invitations go by email, phone alerts and WhatsApp when those are on. Write notes during the meeting; action items become tasks with an owner and a due date. Write summary with AI appears when AI is set up. Clients see meetings they are invited to on their page, say whether they can come and join from there, and can ask for a meeting by suggesting up to three times."},{"u":"browser_extension.html","t":"The browser extension","s":"Your timer in Chrome, Edge and Firefox: start, stop and add tasks from the toolbar and from GitHub, Jira, Trello, Asana, Google Docs and Gmail.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"extension chrome edge firefox toolbar timer badge github jira trello asana google docs gmail connect code idle","b":"Install Handlark: timer and tasks from the Firefox Add ons site or Microsoft Edge Add ons, or from the Chrome Web Store when it is listed there. Until then, your administrator can load it unpacked from the Handlark folder (see extension/README.md ). In Handlark, open your account (owners: Settings, This device) and choose Browser extension , then Show a code . In the extension, open its settings and type the 10 character code. It works once, for 10 minutes. Pin the extension to the toolbar. Before it is used, the extension shows the workspace and the name the code belongs to. Choose Yes, connect only if both are yours; if someone sent you the code, choose Cancel . Until you choose, the connection does nothing, and if you close the settings without choosing it is cancelled after 10 minutes. Type the code only into the extension in your own browser, and never read it to anyone. You see each connected browser in Handlark with its computer, such as Chrome on Windows, and can disconnect it there at any time. Instead of a code you can paste a personal API token, but only one with just tasks, time and clients ticked; a token that can do more is refused. Toolbar: pick a client and a task and start the timer; the badge shows how long it has run. Stop it with an optional line on what you did. New task: add a task for today and start it in one go. Today: your tasks due today, overdue or in progress. Still working: the badge shows a question mark and you can answer from the popup. In the extension settings, turn on the sites you use: GitHub issues and pull requests, Jira, Trello, Asana, Google Docs, Sheets and Slides, and Gmail. The browser asks you for each site. A small Start timer button then appears on an issue, card, task, document or email; pressing it finds the Handlark task linked to that page, or makes one with the page's title and link, and starts your timer. Nothing is read from a page until you press its button. Your token is kept encrypted in the browser, where the pages the extension adds buttons to cannot read it. The extension never captures your screen, never reads your history or other tabs, and has no analytics. For a client with Proof mode on, it opens the task in Handlark instead, where you share your screen with consent. The optional idle hint uses only whether the computer is in use, and asks you, privately, what to do with time away."},{"u":"integrations.html","t":"API, webhooks, Slack, Teams, Discord, Zapier and Make","s":"Connect Handlark to the tools you already use, with the same permissions and privacy as the app.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"api token scopes webhook slack teams discord zapier make integration rest","b":"Settings, Integrations, API tokens (members: your account, API tokens): name it, choose a workspace token (owner) or a personal token, and tick what it may do. It is shown once. Read the API guide . Webhooks send signed events to any https address. Chat alerts post to a Slack, Microsoft Teams or Discord channel through an incoming webhook you make in that app. Private tasks never leave, hidden people show as A teammate, leave says when but never why, and quiet hours apply. Each one sends only what the person who added it may see: a manager's webhook gets the time, attendance and leave of the people they look after, and invoice events only with Invoices and client billing . The owner sees who added each one. When that person can no longer manage integrations it is switched off at once, and when they leave, or the API token that made it is revoked, it stops too. Switching it back on makes it yours. Only the person who added it, or the owner, can make a new signing secret. Send again in the delivery log repeats a delivery only to the same address, for the same person, while they may still see what it is about: when a webhook changes hands or address, its earlier deliveries can no longer be sent again. Every send connects to the address that was checked a moment before, so a web address cannot be pointed at a private network in between. Connect Zapier or Make with an API token to create tasks, log time or react to events without code."},{"u":"alerts.html","t":"Phone alerts, WhatsApp and emails","s":"Turn on phone alerts, WhatsApp alerts and replies, the calendar feed, and choose which emails you get.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"alerts push notifications whatsapp email unsubscribe calendar feed reminders daily summary iphone","b":"In your account, under Phone alerts , choose Turn on for this device on each phone or computer. On an iPhone, first add Handlark to the Home Screen (Share, Add to Home Screen) and open it from there. When the owner turns WhatsApp on, add your number in your account and type the six digit code it sends. Reply TASKS, IN, OUT, DONE 2, ADD and more; STOP turns alerts off. HELP lists every command. Any other message you send or forward to the Handlark number, even one from a group, comes back as a suggested task: reply YES to add it, or NO. See WhatsApp group chats into tasks . Switch reminders, the daily summary, weekly reports and meeting emails on or off under Emails in your account. Invitations and security emails always arrive. Every list email has a one click unsubscribe link. Your account has a private calendar link for Google, Apple or Outlook calendar: due tasks, planned starts and approved leave."},{"u":"whatsapp_to_tasks.html","t":"WhatsApp group chats into tasks","s":"Forward a group message to Handlark, or upload a chat you exported, and keep the tasks you choose.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"whatsapp group forward forwarded chat export upload txt zip tasks from chat android iphone yes no","b":"Turn on WhatsApp in your account first (see Phone alerts, WhatsApp and emails ). Then, in any chat or group, press and hold a message, choose Forward and pick the Handlark number. You can also just type the task to Handlark in a sentence. Handlark replies with what it understood, for example: Add this as a task? 'Send Brooks the October report' for you, due Friday 24 Oct, client Brooks Dental. Reply YES to add it, or NO. YES (or OUI) adds it. NO (or NON) drops it. A suggestion waits 30 minutes; a new one replaces it. A forwarded message is only ever a suggestion, never a command, so a forwarded DONE 1 from a group changes nothing. If your number is in more than one workspace, Handlark first asks which one the task is for: reply 1, 2 and so on. Every reply names the workspace. The task notes keep the original message, and its history says it came from WhatsApp. When AI is on, it reads that one message to find the title, the date and an existing client. It never makes a new client. Without AI, the first line of the message is the title, for you, with no date. Very short messages (ok, thanks, an emoji) and answers to Handlark's own messages are not turned into tasks. Pictures, files and other media cannot become tasks; voice notes can. If the message names someone, the task is for them when your role allows it: the owner can give tasks to anyone, a manager or team lead to the people they look after. A member's tasks are for themselves. If you cannot give it to the person named, the task is yours and the reply says why. On Android: open the group, tap the three dots, then More , Export chat and Without media . Save the file or send it to yourself. On iPhone: open the group, tap its name at the top, scroll down to Export Chat and choose Without Media . Save it to Files. You get a .txt file, or a .zip with the chat inside. Either works. Choose New task , then From text , then From a WhatsApp chat , and choose the file. It is read on your device. Choose the period: the last day, 7 days (the default), 30 days, or since a date. If the dates could be either way round, choose day first or month first. What will be sent shows how many messages and senders go to the AI. Phone numbers and emails are taken out first, and a sender saved only as a number shows as Contact 1, Contact 2. At most about 40,000 characters are read; if the period holds more, the most recent messages are kept. Choose Find tasks . Each task shows who it is for (names from the chat are matched to your people), the date, the client and the message it came from. Change who it is for, edit the title, untick what you do not want, then Add . Nothing from the chat is stored. Only the tasks you add are saved, and the history says how many came from a WhatsApp chat. Finding tasks needs AI and counts as one AI request for every part of the chat read, at most three."},{"u":"ai.html","t":"AI summaries and voice notes","s":"Daily AI summaries, tasks from text and voice notes, and what never reaches the AI.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"ai summary voice note transcribe from text anthropic groq daily summary","b":"When AI is set up, owners get Write summary for the team or one client, everyone gets From text to turn a message or a voice note into tasks, and meetings get a summary with action items. Each workspace has 60 AI requests a day. Private tasks, private lists, and the work, hours and leave of hidden people are left out of every request. Your data is never used to train AI. Voice notes are turned into text and never stored."},{"u":"languages.html","t":"Languages","s":"Use Handlark in English or French, and send clients emails in their language.","c":"Insights, meetings and connections","k":"language french francais english translate","b":"Handlark follows your browser's language at first. To choose, open your account (owners: Settings) and pick Language : follow my browser, English or Français. The app reloads in that language on every device you use, and your emails follow it. In version 1.15.0: the navigation, Home, the task sheet, the time clock, the client page, your account and help, and the main emails (invitations, new tasks, the still working check, leave, meetings, payslips, client summaries, weekly reports, invoices and reminders). Other screens are still in English while we translate them; anything not yet translated shows in English, never blank. The client page follows the client's own browser. Set the language of a client's emails on the client under Settings, Clients ."},{"u":"billing.html","t":"Plans and billing","s":"Plans, the free trial, paying in naira or dollars, changing or cancelling, refunds and referral free months.","c":"Billing, security and your data","k":"plan price starter team agency trial paystack lemon squeezy cancel change card refund referral yearly invoice receipt","b":"Every plan has every feature, priced per workspace, not per person, monthly or yearly. A year costs 10 months, so you get 2 months free. The starting prices are: Starter (up to 5 people): $ 15 or ₦ 12,000 a month, or $ 150 or ₦ 120,000 a year Team (up to 15 people): $ 39 or ₦ 30,000 a month, or $ 390 or ₦ 300,000 a year Agency (up to 50 people): $ 99 or ₦ 75,000 a month, or $ 990 or ₦ 750,000 a year The free trial allows up to 15 people. The prices today, and any founding offer, are on the sales page and under Settings, Plan and billing . A price change only ever applies to new subscribers: once you subscribe, you keep the price you signed up at. While a founding offer runs, the sales page and Settings, Plan and billing show the percent off, the end date and the spots left. Subscribe while it is on and the discount stays on your workspace for life, also when you change plan later. A spot is held for 2 hours while you are at the payment page. The owner pays under Settings, Plan and billing : in naira with Paystack (card, transfer or USSD) or in US dollars with Lemon Squeezy. Cancel plan , Resume plan , Change plan and Update card are all there. The workspace becomes read only: nothing is deleted, and everyone can still export what they can see. Choose a plan to carry on. A full refund within 7 days of the first paid charge (see Refunds ). Share your link under Settings, Refer and earn : the business you invite gets 44 free days, and you get a free month when they pay."},{"u":"security.html","t":"Security and signing in","s":"Two step sign in, sign in with Google or Microsoft, signing out everywhere, and keeping your account safe.","c":"Billing, security and your data","k":"security two step sign in 2fa authenticator google microsoft password reset sign out everywhere trust device","b":"In your account, turn on two step sign in with an authenticator app and keep the recovery codes. Owners can require it for everyone under Settings, Security . After 5 wrong codes, codes pause for 15 minutes. Continue with Google and Continue with Microsoft appear when the business that runs your Handlark switched them on. An existing account is linked only when the provider confirmed the same email, after you type your password once. Sign out everywhere in your account signs out every phone and computer at once, this one too. On shared computers, leave Trust this device off. Read the security page and the trust centre ."},{"u":"data.html","t":"Your data: export, history and deleting","s":"Export everything as spreadsheets, the history of changes, leaving a workspace, deleting your account or a workspace.","c":"Billing, security and your data","k":"export csv zip history audit delete account delete workspace leave restore retention","b":"Owners: Settings, Export everything downloads a ZIP of spreadsheets. Everyone else: Export what I can see in their account. Both work even after a trial ends. The owner sees every change with what it was before and after, filtered by person, words and dates. Secrets never appear in it. Leave this workspace deletes your profile there; your shared work stays. Delete my account needs your password. The owner can delete a workspace and restore it for 30 days; after that it is purged. See the data retention table ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html","t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Fixes for the usual problems: offline changes, alerts that do not arrive, sign in, uploads, a stopped timer and a read only workspace.","c":"Troubleshooting and support","k":"problem not working offline sync alerts not arriving iphone sign in loop upload failed timer stopped read only email not received spam","b":"Changes made offline are kept on the device and sent when you reconnect; a banner says how many are waiting. Keep the tab open until it says you are back online. Files can only be added while online. Check alerts are on in your account on this device, and allowed for the site in your browser or phone settings. On an iPhone, alerts work only from the Home Screen app. Quiet hours hold alerts until your working day starts. Use Forgot your password? on the sign in screen. If your workspace requires two step sign in, have your authenticator app ready, or use a recovery code. After many wrong codes, wait 15 minutes. Timers stop past 10 hours or 2 hours past your working day, and time pauses when the still working check got no answer. Claim the time with a note under Insights, Time, My week . The trial or plan has ended. The owner chooses a plan under Settings, Plan and billing . Nothing is deleted meanwhile. Look in spam and promotions. Check that your email is right under your account and that you did not unsubscribe from those emails. The owner can see whether email is set up under Settings. Under Help and support, Report a problem , an email opens with your app version and device filled in."},{"u":"contact.html","t":"Contact support","s":"Email, WhatsApp and live chat with the Handlark team, and what to include so we can help quickly.","c":"Troubleshooting and support","k":"contact support help chat whatsapp email live chat status","b":"Email us from Help and support in the app or the button below. When the team offers them, WhatsApp and live chat are there too; live chat opens in a new tab. What you did, what you expected, what happened, and a screenshot if you can. Report a problem fills in your app version and device for you. Check the service status page ."}];
